      "result": "\n\nDone. The complete Zephyr application is written to `submission/main.c`:\n\n- **Message struct** — `struct message` with an `int32_t value`\n- **Bounded message queue** — `K_MSGQ_DEFINE(msgq, sizeof(struct message), 8, 1)` (holds 8 messages)\n- **Producer thread** — puts incrementing values with a 200 ms `k_sleep` between sends, retrying with a bounded timeout if the queue is full\n- **Consumer thread** — blocks on `k_msgq_get(..., K_FOREVER)` and logs each value\n- **Priorities** — producer at 5 (higher), consumer at 7\n- **Static definition** — both threads use `K_THREAD_STACK_DEFINE` + `K_THREAD_DEFINE`\n- **main()** — logs startup, then loops forever with `k_sleep` while the threads run\n\nIt uses `LOG_MODULE_REGISTER`/`LOG_INF` (modern Zephyr logging) so it builds against a standard Zephyr application with no extra configuration needed.",
